@startuml
title E2EE OrgBot and Protected Export
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #334155
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF7D6
  DiamondBorderColor #A16207
}

start
:Export administrator selects room scope;
:Export page signs in through Keycloak using OIDC + PKCE;
:Export Service verifies signed claims using Keycloak JWKS;
:Reload current room map and authorization policy;
if (matrix-access, org-export-admin and current requested scope allowed?) then (yes)
  :Send exact room IDs to OrgBot over its private endpoint;
  :OrgBot uses content from its continuous non-admin Matrix sync;
  note right
    OrgBot is joined to approved encrypted rooms as a PL 0
    participant and uses its own persistent E2EE device store.
    Its session-only volume is separate from the Policy Sync
    administrator-token volume. OrgBot has no room-admin role.

    Policy Sync's private administrator creates managed rooms
    and controls membership/security state, not E2EE content.
    In v12 the creator has immutable power and is absent from
    the power-level `users` map. For v11 with a power-level
    event, creator power is `users[creator]` or `users_default`.
  end note
  :Decrypt only content available to OrgBot's own device;
  :Package observed events and available attachments in a ZIP;
  :Recheck current actor, entitlement and exact scope before delivery;
  :Return archive, completeness status and audit digest;
else (no)
  :Reject before requesting content from OrgBot;
endif
stop

note right
  Archives describe observed/decrypted content. Missing history,
  keys or media remain visible as gaps; current status is partial.

  Verify encrypted messages and attachments with a synthetic
  end-to-end fixture. The bot does not backfill history, and an
  archive can be partial even when its ZIP is valid.
end note
@enduml
